WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.012
Gate two is Microsoft 365.

2
00:00:03.012 --> 00:00:07.200
The message center is where Microsoft
announces changes, retirements and

3
00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:11.251
actions for a tenant, and service
health lists incidents and advisories.

4
00:00:11.251 --> 00:00:15.400
Microsoft Graph's service
communications API reads both.

5
00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:19.900
Two steps: sign in to the tenant's
own cloud with two read permissions,

6
00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:23.275
and collect three lists,
following every next link.

7
00:00:23.275 --> 00:00:27.982
Microsoft Learn says both permissions
are granted only by an administrator,

8
00:00:27.982 --> 00:00:30.850
and a delegated sign-in
also needs an admin role.

9
00:00:30.850 --> 00:00:34.015
Data privacy messages are
visible only to Global

10
00:00:34.015 --> 00:00:37.412
Administrators and Message
Center Privacy Readers.

11
00:00:37.412 --> 00:00:38.475
Now the cloud.

12
00:00:38.475 --> 00:00:41.843
A GCC tenant keeps the
worldwide Graph endpoint,

13
00:00:41.843 --> 00:00:44.875
which Learn's national
cloud page confirms.

14
00:00:44.875 --> 00:00:48.513
GCC High and the Defense
Department have their own hosts,

15
00:00:48.513 --> 00:00:52.150
and the workbook's capture shows
the kit's map of all three.

16
00:00:52.150 --> 00:00:55.366
The kit sends each call only
to the cloud's own host,

17
00:00:55.366 --> 00:00:59.040
and refuses a session in
another environment or tenant.
